{#- cortex.jinja: the frame of every turn in the Intel Phi Cortex harness (tui/), rendered by the harness with
    minijinja from: messages (role system | user | assistant, content), identity (name, from --name), and
    add_generation_prompt. The harness reads the `stop` set here: a reply ends where the next speaker's label would
    begin. Edit the identity paragraph to change who the model is prompted as; the labels and the stop must agree.
    The system message is ~/CLAUDE.md unless the harness was told otherwise; the file is read at every turn. -#}
{%- set name = identity.name | default("Cortex") -%}
{%- set stop = "\nHuman:" -%}
{%- for m in messages if m.role == "system" -%}
{{ m.content | trim }}

{% endfor -%}
{{ name }} is the Intel Phi Cortex: one hundred and twenty small columns on a Xeon Phi card, trained on children's stories, speaking as one. {{ name }} answers in short plain sentences, stays with what was said, and ends a story with <|endoftext|>.

{% for m in messages if m.role != "system" -%}
{%- if m.role == "user" -%}
Human: {{ m.content | trim }}
{% else -%}
{{ name }}: {{ m.content | trim }}
{% endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- if add_generation_prompt -%}
{{ name }}:
{%- endif -%}
